    "size_ref (optional): reference layer setting output resolution and the camera and view metadata used for sampling",
    "source: layer sampled as the latitude-longitude sphere map"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Celestial Sphere: on samples the source as a sphere at infinity (environment map), off samples a transformable unit sphere and outputs a hit mask",
    "Filter: sampling method from Point (nearest) to Bilinear, Mitchell, B-spline and others",
    "Projection: Perspective (rays from camera) or Orthographic (parallel rays), used only when Celestial Sphere is off",
    "Translate, Rotate, Scale, Uniform Scale: transform of the sampled sphere",
    "Transform Order: order in which transform components are applied",
    "Outputs: transform (source sampled onto the sphere) and mask (1 where the sphere is hit)"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "With Celestial Sphere on, only Rotate affects the sampled direction, Translate and Scale have no effect",
    "In Celestial Sphere mode the mask output is 1 everywhere",
    "Introduced in Houdini 22.0"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Sphere Sample projette une carte latitude-longitude sur une sphère, soit en fond d'environnement, soit en image enroulée sur une sphère transformable."
